<title>USA: Novartis ADRs start trading on Nasdaq.</title>
<headline>Novartis ADRs start trading on Nasdaq.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Novartis AG on Monday said its American Depositary Receipts have started trading on the Nasdaq over-the-counter market under the symbol &quot;NWTSY.&quot;</p>
<p>Each ADR represents 1/20 of an ordinary share of the company, Novartis said.</p>
<p>The company, with a market capitalization of about $85 billion, is the second-largest pharamaceutical company worldwide and the third-largest company in Europe. It was formed by the merger of Ciba-Geigy and Sandoz.</p>
</text>
